4. Why not combineByKey() or map() + reduceByKey()?
========================================================================
combineByKey(first_review, add_review, merge_boxes) same answer? True
one-review boxes (first 2): [('grinder', [0, 0, 0, 0, 1]), ('kettle', [0, 0, 0, 1, 0])]
mapValues(one_review_box).reduceByKey(merge_boxes)  same answer? True

========================================================================
5. A common mistake: a zeroValue that is not empty
========================================================================
[('grinder', [0, 0, 1, 1, 4]), ('kettle', [0, 1, 0, 2, 2]), ('mug', [0, 0, 0, 0, 2])]
mug got ONE free 5-star review (its reviews are in one partition),
but grinder and kettle got TWO (their reviews are in two partitions).
Business rules like 'add a bonus' belong AFTER the aggregation
(in mapValues()), never in the zeroValue.
